  "id": "level-of-analysis",
  "term": "level of analysis",
  "definition": "Level of analysis refers to how deeply data are interpreted in a study, such as examining underlying ideas and meanings rather than staying with a more surface descriptive account. In qualitative research, a more latent level of analysis usually involves more intensive work with each transcript or case.",
